{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_81","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat engine/crates/pav_core/build.rs | head -155; stat -c '%y %n' notes/test-core.log notes/test-audio-ui.log engine/assets/props/lib/core/fit_tray.json; tail -20 notes/core-result.log; ps --ppid 3953139 -o pid,etime,time,args; tail -15 build-web.log\"","aggregated_output":"// Embeds every room file in /rooms into the binary (rooms.rs in OUT_DIR), so adding a room\n// file is enough for it to ship; likewise game data, animation data and the embedded assets.\nuse std::io::Write;\n\nfn main() {\n    // A folder that can't be read would embed nothing and fail much later, far from the cause.\n    for data in [\"rooms\", \"game\", \"anim\"] {\n        let path = std::path::Path::new(env!(\"CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR\")).join(\"../..\").join(data);\n        assert!(path.is_dir(), \"{} is missing: pav_core embeds the repository's /{data} folder\", path.display());\n    }\n    let dir = std::path::Path::new(env!(\"CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR\")).join(\"../../rooms\");\n    println!(\"cargo:rerun-if-changed={}\", dir.display());\n    let mut entries: Vec<_> = std::fs::read_dir(&dir)\n        .map(|d| d.filter_map(|e| e.ok()).map(|e| e.path()).filter(|p| p.extension().is_some_and(|x| x == \"toml\")).collect())\n        .unwrap_or_default();\n    entries.sort();\n    let out = std::path::Path::new(&std::env::var(\"OUT_DIR\").unwrap()).join(\"rooms.rs\");\n    let mut f = std::fs::File::create(out).unwrap();\n    writeln!(f, \"pub const EMBEDDED: &[(&str, &str)] = &[\").unwrap();\n    for p in entries {\n        println!(\"cargo:rerun-if-changed={}\", p.display());\n        let stem = p.file_stem().unwrap().to_string_lossy().to_string();\n        let abs = p.canonicalize().unwrap();\n        writeln!(f, \"    ({stem:?}, include_str!({:?})),\", abs.display().to_string()).unwrap();\n    }\n    writeln!(f, \"];\").unwrap();\n\n    // Game data (Shardfall): every .toml under /game, keyed by its path relative to /game\n    // without the extension (\"skills\", \"levels/01_shrines\").\n    let game = std::path::Path::new(env!(\"CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR\")).join(\"../../game\");\n    println!(\"cargo:rerun-if-changed={}\", game.display());\n    let mut files = Vec::new();\n    collect(&game, &mut files);\n    files.sort();\n    let out = std::path::Path::new(&std::env::var(\"OUT_DIR\").unwrap()).join(\"game_data.rs\");\n    let mut f = std::fs::File::create(out).unwrap();\n    writeln!(f, \"pub const GAME_DATA: &[(&str, &str)] = &[\").unwrap();\n    for p in files {\n        println!(\"cargo:rerun-if-changed={}\", p.display());\n        let rel = p.strip_prefix(&game).unwrap().with_extension(\"\");\n        let key = rel.to_string_lossy().replace('\\\\', \"/\");\n        let abs = p.canonicalize().unwrap();\n        writeln!(f, \"    ({key:?}, include_str!({:?})),\", abs.display().to_string()).unwrap();\n    }\n    writeln!(f, \"];\").unwrap();\n\n    // Animation data: the files directly in /anim (moves.toml and the clip sets, *.json), keyed by\n    // file name. Sub-folders (the full motion-capture libraries) stay on disk and load on demand.\n    let anim = std::path::Path::new(env!(\"CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR\")).join(\"../../anim\");\n    println!(\"cargo:rerun-if-changed={}\", anim.display());\n    let mut files: Vec<_> = std::fs::read_dir(&anim)\n        .map(|d| {\n            d.filter_map(|e| e.ok())\n                .map(|e| e.path())\n                .filter(|p| p.is_file() && p.extension().is_some_and(|x| x == \"toml\" || x == \"json\"))\n                .collect()\n        })\n        .unwrap_or_default();\n    files.sort();\n    let out = std::path::Path::new(&std::env::var(\"OUT_DIR\").unwrap()).join(\"anim_data.rs\");\n    let mut f = std::fs::File::create(out).unwrap();\n    writeln!(f, \"pub const ANIM_DATA: &[(&str, &str)] = &[\").unwrap();\n    for p in files {\n        println!(\"cargo:rerun-if-changed={}\", p.display());\n        let name = p.file_name().unwrap().to_string_lossy().to_string();\n        let abs = p.canonicalize().unwrap();\n        writeln!(f, \"    ({name:?}, include_str!({:?})),\", abs.display().to_string()).unwrap();\n    }\n    writeln!(f, \"];\").unwrap();\n\n    // Core materials: assets/materials/*.json and pb/*.json, keyed by their name (\"oak_planks\",\n    // \"pb/gold\"), which is `MAT/<name>`. The other tiers (workshop, fit, local) stay on disk.\n    let materials = std::path::Path::new(env!(\"CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR\")).join(\"../../assets/materials\");\n    let mut files = Vec::new();\n    for sub in [\"\", \"pb\"] {\n        let dir = materials.join(sub);\n        println!(\"cargo:rerun-if-changed={}\", dir.display());\n        let Ok(rd) = std::fs::read_dir(&dir) else { continue };\n        for p in rd.filter_map(|e| e.ok()).map(|e| e.path()) {\n            if p.is_file() && p.extension().is_some_and(|x| x == \"json\") {\n                let stem = p.file_stem().unwrap().to_string_lossy().to_string();\n                files.push((if sub.is_empty() { stem } else { format!(\"{sub}/{stem}\") }, p));\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    files.sort();\n    let out = std::path::Path::new(&std::env::var(\"OUT_DIR\").unwrap()).join(\"materials.rs\");\n    let mut f = std::fs::File::create(out).unwrap();\n    writeln!(f, \"pub const MATERIALS: &[(&str, &str)] = &[\").unwrap();\n    for (name, p) in files {\n        println!(\"cargo:rerun-if-changed={}\", p.display());\n        let abs = p.canonicalize().unwrap();\n        writeln!(f, \"    ({name:?}, include_str!({:?})),\", abs.display().to_string()).unwrap();\n    }\n    writeln!(f, \"];\").unwrap();\n\n    // Object assets, the embedded tier (docs/ASSET_SYSTEM_PLAN.md §9.1): the templates and the\n    // core library (assets, meshes, index.tsv), keyed by their path under assets/props, plus the\n    // shipped packs (`props::store::SHIPPED`: files every build carries so rooms can show them,\n    // their rows keeping their own tier). Other packs stay on disk, and local ones on this\n    // machine. A pack's licence (PACK.json) and review ledger (review.tsv) are for tools, not the\n    // game.\n    let props = std::path::Path::new(env!(\"CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR\")).join(\"../../assets/props\");\n    let mut files = Vec::new();\n    for folder in [\"templates\", \"lib/core\", \"lib/kaykit_adventurers\"] {\n        let dir = props.join(folder);\n        if dir.is_dir() {\n            println!(\"cargo:rerun-if-changed={}\", dir.display());\n            collect_ext(&dir, &[\"json\", \"tsv\"], &mut files);\n        }\n    }\n    files.retain(|p| !p.file_name().is_some_and(|n| n == \"PACK.json\" || n == \"review.tsv\"));\n    files.sort();\n    let out = std::path::Path::new(&std::env::var(\"OUT_DIR\").unwrap()).join(\"asset_data.rs\");\n    let mut f = std::fs::File::create(out).unwrap();\n    writeln!(f, \"pub const ASSET_DATA: &[(&str, &str)] = &[\").unwrap();\n    for p in files {\n        let key = p.strip_prefix(&props).unwrap().to_string_lossy().replace('\\\\', \"/\");\n        let abs = p.canonicalize().unwrap();\n        writeln!(f, \"    ({key:?}, include_str!({:?})),\", abs.display().to_string()).unwrap();\n    }\n    writeln!(f, \"];\").unwrap();\n}\n\n/// Files under `dir` with one of `extensions`, skipping hidden files and folders.\nfn collect_ext(dir: &std::path::Path, extensions: &[&str], out: &mut Vec<std::path::PathBuf>) {\n    let Ok(rd) = std::fs::read_dir(dir) else { return };\n    for e in rd.filter_map(|e| e.ok()) {\n        let p = e.path();\n        if p.file_name().is_some_and(|n| n.to_string_lossy().starts_with('.')) {\n            continue;\n        }\n        if p.is_dir() {\n            collect_ext(&p, extensions, out);\n        } else if p.extension().is_some_and(|x| extensions.iter().any(|e| x == *e)) {\n            out.push(p);\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nfn collect(dir: &std::path::Path, out: &mut Vec<std::path::PathBuf>) {\n    let Ok(rd) = std::fs::read_dir(dir) else { return };\n    for e in rd.filter_map(|e| e.ok()) {\n        let p = e.path();\n        if p.is_dir() {\n            println!(\"cargo:rerun-if-changed={}\", p.display());\n            collect(&p, out);\n        } else if p.extension().is_some_and(|x| x == \"toml\") {\n            out.push(p);\n        }\n    }\n}\n2026-11-04 23:01:05.713028473 -0700 notes/test-core.log\n2026-11-04 23:03:14.579885463 -0700 notes/test-audio-ui.log\n2026-11-04 22:58:01.683404608 -0700 engine/assets/props/lib/core/fit_tray.json\n18 passed, 0 failed\n    PID     ELAPSED     TIME COMMAND\n   Compiling pav_core v0.1.0 (/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max.build-v2__20261104-222458__x35112d/work/Wobble-Wit-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261104-222458/engine/crates/pav_core)\n   Compiling pav_audio v0.1.0 (/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max.build-v2__20261104-222458__x35112d/work/Wobble-Wit-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261104-222458/engine/crates/pav_audio)\n   Compiling pav_ui v0.1.0 (/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max.build-v2__20261104-222458__x35112d/work/Wobble-Wit-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261104-222458/engine/crates/pav_ui)\n   Compiling pav_view v0.1.0 (/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max.build-v2__20261104-222458__x35112d/work/Wobble-Wit-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261104-222458/engine/crates/pav_view)\n   Compiling pav_tools v0.1.0 (/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max.build-v2__20261104-222458__x35112d/work/Wobble-Wit-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261104-222458/engine/crates/pav_tools)\n   Compiling pav_app v0.1.0 (/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max.build-v2__20261104-222458__x35112d/work/Wobble-Wit-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261104-222458/engine/crates/pav_app)\n    Finished `dist` profile [optimized] target(s) in 1m 16s\n/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max.build-v2__20261104-222458__x35112d/work/Wobble-Wit-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261104-222458/engine/../../Wobble-Wit-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261104-222458.html: 11.7 MB (wasm 29.0 MB, gzipped 8.7 MB; JS glue 0.1 MB)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
