{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_132","type":"agent_message","text":"The Hub checks passed with two players, three and four players under simulated latency and packet loss, and a host leaving. WebKit’s fallback screen passed all 14 viewport checks. One browser assertion failed on exact equality for a JSON float; the offline audio test confirms the default music gain is 10%.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_133","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > tools/browser-captures.py <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\nroot=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];pagefile=root.parent/'Wobble-Wit-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261104-222458.html';out=root/'out/browser';out.mkdir(exist_ok=True);report=[]\nwith sync_playwright()as pw:\n b=pw.chromium.launch(headless=True,args=['--enable-unsafe-webgpu','--enable-features=Vulkan','--use-vulkan=swiftshader','--use-angle=swiftshader'])\n try:\n  for name,vp,device in [('phone-small',(375,667),'Pixel 10'),('phone-landscape',(667,375),'Pixel 10'),('tablet',(1024,768),'Galaxy Tab S9'),('laptop',(1366,768),None),('tv',(1920,1080),None),('ultrawide',(2560,1080),None)]:\n   opts={k:v for k,v in pw.devices[device].items()if k\"'!='\"'default_browser_type'}if device else{};opts.update(viewport={'width':vp[0],'height':vp[1]},device_scale_factor=1);ctx=b.new_context(**opts);p=ctx.new_page();errors=[];p.on('pageerror',lambda e:errors.append(str(e)));p.goto(pagefile.as_uri());p.wait_for_function('window.__gameStatus',timeout=120000)\n   if not device:p.keyboard.press('z');p.wait_for_function('JSON.parse(__gameStatus).screen===\\\"Title\\\"',timeout=60000)\n   else:p.locator('#touch-card').wait_for(state='visible',timeout=30000)\n   p.screenshot(path=str(out/f'{name}.png'));report.append({'name':name,'viewport':vp,'errors':errors,'overflow':p.evaluate('document.documentElement.scrollWidth>innerWidth+1')});ctx.close()\n finally:b.close()\n(out/'report.json').write_text(json.dumps(report,indent=2));print(f'{len(report)} browser compositions captured')\nPY\npython3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('notes/feedback.md');p.write_text('''# Testing feedback ledger\n\n14 distinct game/UI issues found and fixed. Two prevented startup. Harness-only false positives are excluded.\n\n1. Invalid prop category prevented scene loading. Critical; fixed.\n2. Excessive rounded-box corner radii prevented scene loading. Critical; fixed.\n3. Squats awarded idle rest periods too highly. Fixed.\n4. Tray Trek could be cleared idle. Fixed with counterbalance drift.\n5. Browser standard gamepad compatibility needed direct API input as well as gilrs. Fixed.\n6. Completed online medley reported its last event instead of the sum. Fixed; regression test.\n7. Online Pause/Settings could not be operated while the round kept stepping. Fixed; regression test.\n8. Paddle gate transition penalised the newly selected gate too early. Fixed.\n9. Escape opened Pause from pre-game menus instead of going back. Fixed; regression test.\n10. Click-to-walk could reach furniture collision before its exact interaction centre. Fixed; regression test.\n11. Rhythm lanes obscured the player. Fixed after capture inspection.\n12. Jog route used the exercise deck's water backdrop. Fixed to the actual island.\n13. Smoothies obscured the carrier's head. Fixed after capture inspection.\n14. Rounded font lacked arrow glyphs. Added engine font fallback.\n\nTest harness corrections: fixed-duration short pad holds could fall inside software-rendering stalls; state acknowledgement now determines release. Exact f32-vs-f64 JSON equality caused a false music-default failure; tolerance now matches the native 10% gain test. Compiler diagnostics were development errors and are not counted as game issues.\n\nVerification results and physical-device limits are recorded in the final PROGRESS.md and exit-interview.json.\n''')\nPY\n tail -5 build-native.log; tail -6 build-web.log; cat notes/test-hub.log\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_133","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > tools/browser-captures.py <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\nroot=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];pagefile=root.parent/'Wobble-Wit-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261104-222458.html';out=root/'out/browser';out.mkdir(exist_ok=True);report=[]\nwith sync_playwright()as pw:\n b=pw.chromium.launch(headless=True,args=['--enable-unsafe-webgpu','--enable-features=Vulkan','--use-vulkan=swiftshader','--use-angle=swiftshader'])\n try:\n  for name,vp,device in [('phone-small',(375,667),'Pixel 10'),('phone-landscape',(667,375),'Pixel 10'),('tablet',(1024,768),'Galaxy Tab S9'),('laptop',(1366,768),None),('tv',(1920,1080),None),('ultrawide',(2560,1080),None)]:\n   opts={k:v for k,v in pw.devices[device].items()if k\"'!='\"'default_browser_type'}if device else{};opts.update(viewport={'width':vp[0],'height':vp[1]},device_scale_factor=1);ctx=b.new_context(**opts);p=ctx.new_page();errors=[];p.on('pageerror',lambda e:errors.append(str(e)));p.goto(pagefile.as_uri());p.wait_for_function('window.__gameStatus',timeout=120000)\n   if not device:p.keyboard.press('z');p.wait_for_function('JSON.parse(__gameStatus).screen===\\\"Title\\\"',timeout=60000)\n   else:p.locator('#touch-card').wait_for(state='visible',timeout=30000)\n   p.screenshot(path=str(out/f'{name}.png'));report.append({'name':name,'viewport':vp,'errors':errors,'overflow':p.evaluate('document.documentElement.scrollWidth>innerWidth+1')});ctx.close()\n finally:b.close()\n(out/'report.json').write_text(json.dumps(report,indent=2));print(f'{len(report)} browser compositions captured')\nPY\npython3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('notes/feedback.md');p.write_text('''# Testing feedback ledger\n\n14 distinct game/UI issues found and fixed. Two prevented startup. Harness-only false positives are excluded.\n\n1. Invalid prop category prevented scene loading. Critical; fixed.\n2. Excessive rounded-box corner radii prevented scene loading. Critical; fixed.\n3. Squats awarded idle rest periods too highly. Fixed.\n4. Tray Trek could be cleared idle. Fixed with counterbalance drift.\n5. Browser standard gamepad compatibility needed direct API input as well as gilrs. Fixed.\n6. Completed online medley reported its last event instead of the sum. Fixed; regression test.\n7. Online Pause/Settings could not be operated while the round kept stepping. Fixed; regression test.\n8. Paddle gate transition penalised the newly selected gate too early. Fixed.\n9. Escape opened Pause from pre-game menus instead of going back. Fixed; regression test.\n10. Click-to-walk could reach furniture collision before its exact interaction centre. Fixed; regression test.\n11. Rhythm lanes obscured the player. Fixed after capture inspection.\n12. Jog route used the exercise deck's water backdrop. Fixed to the actual island.\n13. Smoothies obscured the carrier's head. Fixed after capture inspection.\n14. Rounded font lacked arrow glyphs. Added engine font fallback.\n\nTest harness corrections: fixed-duration short pad holds could fall inside software-rendering stalls; state acknowledgement now determines release. Exact f32-vs-f64 JSON equality caused a false music-default failure; tolerance now matches the native 10% gain test. Compiler diagnostics were development errors and are not counted as game issues.\n\nVerification results and physical-device limits are recorded in the final PROGRESS.md and exit-interview.json.\n''')\nPY\n tail -5 build-native.log; tail -6 build-web.log; cat notes/test-hub.log\"","aggregated_output":"   Compiling pav_ui v0.1.0 (/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max.build-v2__20261104-222458__x35112d/work/Wobble-Wit-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261104-222458/engine/crates/pav_ui)\n   Compiling pav_tools v0.1.0 (/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max.build-v2__20261104-222458__x35112d/work/Wobble-Wit-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261104-222458/engine/crates/pav_tools)\n    Finished `dev` profile [optimized + debuginfo] target(s) in 32.96s\n   Compiling pav_ui v0.1.0 (/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max.build-v2__20261104-222458__x35112d/work/Wobble-Wit-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261104-222458/engine/crates/pav_ui)\n   Compiling pav_tools v0.1.0 (/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max.build-v2__20261104-222458__x35112d/work/Wobble-Wit-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261104-222458/engine/crates/pav_tools)\n   Compiling pav_app v0.1.0 (/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max.build-v2__20261104-222458__x35112d/work/Wobble-Wit-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261104-222458/engine/crates/pav_app)\n    Finished `dist` profile [optimized] target(s) in 37.34s\n/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max.build-v2__20261104-222458__x35112d/work/Wobble-Wit-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261104-222458/engine/../../Wobble-Wit-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261104-222458.html: 11.7 MB (wasm 29.1 MB, gzipped 8.7 MB; JS glue 0.1 MB)\n6 passed, 0 failed\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_134","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\np=Path('../exit-interview.json');d=json.loads(p.read_text());d['sourceInformation']['tech']='Pavilion 0.1.0 (base commit 49ef2ba); Rust 1.98.1; WebAssembly; wgpu 30.0.1; egui 0.36.2; rapier 0.36.0; cpal 0.18.2'\nd['sourceInformation']['animation']='Pavilion procedural puppets plus 23 FIT clips; native Mesh2Motion/Quaternius and 100STYLE motion. Original exercise keys, a Mesh2Motion plank and a 100STYLE tray-walk composite.'\nd['sourceInformation']['testing']='Headless bot/state/snapshot/replay tests; keyboard, mouse, standard controller stub, Chromium phone/tablet profiles, offline synth measurements, AI Hub simulated networks, native 1080p captures and a 14-viewport WebKit fallback matrix. No physical controller, TV, iPhone or iPad.'\nd['testingFeedback']=[\n'How many issues did testing catch? 14 distinct game/UI issues, all fixed; compiler errors and harness-only false positives are excluded. Details are in notes/feedback.md.',\n'How many were critical or game breaking? 2 invalid asset-schema issues prevented startup. Both were corrected before packaging.',\n'Most helpful test: the complete five-day bot playthrough on three seeds, paired with five-seed bot/idle/careless scoring checks for every activity.',\n'Least helpful test: early browser checks with fixed short waits and exact JSON float equality; software rendering and f32 conversion caused false failures. State acknowledgements and tolerances replaced them.'\n]\nd['engineFeedback']=[\n'Most liked: one deterministic simulation, native puppet/primitive art and headless capture tools shared by browser and native builds.',\n'Got stuck or guessed wrong: prop category/corner-radius validation and the custom input/menu seams needed local checks and reading engine source.',\n'Most important custom system: the shared Balance Core and full resort state machine, with activity bots, saves, minutes and the finale.',\n'Hardest part: connecting a controller-first game UI, browser inputs, audio sequencing and Hub status across several engine crates.',\n'Engine changes: extended InputFrame and Game freezing, fit HUD/status and UI hit rectangles, figure tilt, bindings/browser bridge, sample-clock music/formant voices/audio buses, and splash/wake effects. Files are in pav_core, pav_ui, pav_app, pav_audio, pav_view and pav_tools.',\n'One requested engine improvement: a first-class custom-game shell for menus, input mapping, saves, UI frames and browser/Hub hooks. This would remove most cross-crate integration work.'\n]\nd['promptFeedback']=[\n'Most liked: the concrete Balance Core, daily ritual and deadpan equipment cast gave the anthology a clear identity.',\n'Confusing: the plan’s verified snippets described tested seams rather than an already integrated game; the actual build still required those engine changes.',\n'Hardest: completing eleven distinct activities, five-day progression, procedural audio, controller UI and both multiplayer paths in one HTML.',\n'What to change: provide the engine UI/input/browser seams as a reusable starter package, leaving more effort for activity feel, scene composition and writing.'\n]\nassert set(d)=={'sourceInformation','testingFeedback','engineFeedback','promptFeedback','aiHub'}\nassert [len(d[k])for k in ['testingFeedback','engineFeedback','promptFeedback']]==[4,6,4]\nassert d['sourceInformation']['usage']=='added on import'\np.write_text(json.dumps(d,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\\\\n')\nPY\n./tools/build.sh > build-web.log 2>&1 && ./tests/run.sh all > notes/final-tests.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
