M decompression/magic, About/interview equality, Hub client and license block validated in dev/notes/package-check.json.\n- No physical controller, TV or real iOS device was available. Controller/audio/touch stand-ins used. WebKit tested the WebGPU-required fallback, not real iOS Safari gameplay.\n\n## Rebuild and extend\n- `cd {base.name} && tools/build.sh` rebuilds the exact root HTML and imports exit-interview.json.\n- `tests/run.sh [core|browser|hub|all]` prints failures and one count.\n- Fit game: engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit; UI: pav_ui/src/fit_ui.rs; browser bridge: pav_app/src/weblink.rs; synth arrangements/voices: pav_audio/src/music.rs and voice.rs.\n- Rules, dialogue, charts and sets are editable TOML; props and clips are readable JSON. See dev/README.md.\n- Build/download/staging caches removed after verification: engine/target, fonts-download, hub-test and Python bytecode. Source, test harness, notes, licenses and capture evidence remain.\n\nNo required work remains. No sub-agents were used. No public tunnel was created.\n'\"'''\n(root/'PROGRESS.md').write_text(progress)\nprint('Build caches removed; source, evidence and final deliverables retained.')\nprint('HTML checksum unchanged:',hashlib.sha256(page.read_bytes()).hexdigest())\nPY\nls -lh ../Wobble-Wit-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261104-222458.html ../exit-interview.json ../PROGRESS.md\n du -sh .\"","aggregated_output":"Build caches removed; source, evidence and final deliverables retained.\nHTML checksum unchanged: 432929aae2266a828b50ee2f1d8e568addc35a8aa10cbde6c1dc924f149e59ce\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 4.1K Nov  5 00:13 ../PROGRESS.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  12M Nov  5 00:04 ../Wobble-Wit-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261104-222458.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 4.3K Nov  5 00:03 ../exit-interview.json\n115M\t.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_161","type":"agent_message","text":"Built **[Wobble Wit](​/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max.build-v2__20261104-222458__x35112d/work/Wobble-Wit-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261104-222458.html)** — a self-contained 11.7 MB game. Open it in a WebGPU-capable browser with a controller or keyboard.\n\n**58 checks passed.** Source, tests, captures, [progress notes](/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max.build-v2__20261104-222458__x35112d/work/PROGRESS.md), and the [exit interview](/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max.build-v2__20261104-222458__x35112d/work/exit-interview.json) are included. Build caches were removed.\n\n**Source Information:** Date: 2026-11-04 22:24:58. Source: Wii Fit. Plan: PLAN.md. Genre: Sports. Perspective: third person, with activity-specific cameras. Tech: [Pavilion](https://github.com/michaelcrosato/shardfall/blob/main/START_HERE.md) 0.1.0, Rust 1.98.1, WASM/WebGPU, wgpu 30.0.1, egui 0.36.2, rapier 0.36.0 and cpal 0.18.2. Art: pastel cel-shaded primitives. Animation: native puppets and 23 FIT clips. Audio: synthesised music, effects and gibberish voices; music defaults to 10%. Online: [AI Hub](https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub) ghost sessions and local hot-seat multiplayer. Research: engine and Hub documentation. Testing: headless scripts and device stand-ins. Environment: Codex CLI, headless Linux. Model: OpenAI gpt-6.1-sol, reasoning effort max. Usage: added on import.\n\n**Testing Feedback:** Found and fixed 16 issues; two prevented startup. Most helpful: complete five-day bot playthroughs and event scoring comparisons. Least helpful: short fixed browser waits, replaced by state acknowledgements. Fourteen WebKit viewport checks passed for the fallback screen. Physical controller, TV and iOS testing were unavailable.\n\n**Engine Feedback:** The shared simulation and capture tools worked well. Prop schemas and menu routing needed correction. The largest custom system was the Balance Core and resort flow. Integrating UI, audio and browser input across crates was hardest. Engine changes cover input, pause, HUD, tilt, audio, effects and browser/Hub hooks. A reusable custom-game shell would help most.\n\n**Prompt Feedback:** The concrete mechanics and cast were helpful. Verified snippets still required integration. Completing the anthology and multiplayer was hardest. Providing reusable UI, input, save and browser hooks would improve the prompt."}}
